{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Shall I conceal… and Abraham shall become.</b> He said: were he not destined to beget children, I would not reveal to him the judgment of Sodom, for what does a man who will die without children — that he should command them to keep the way of HaShem and receive reward — have to do with revealing judgments? But 'Abraham shall become' etc. 'For I have known him' etc. And since he will become a great nation, I will reveal to him the judgment of Sodom, 'for I have known him' — that on account of the judgment I will execute upon these wicked ones, he will command his children to keep the way of HaShem, to do righteousness and justice." "<b>In order that HaShem may bring etc.</b> And they will merit inheriting the land, for if they do not keep justice and righteousness, they will not merit this."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:33.656096407Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}